#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""solo-verify — gate evaluator for the Solo Claude Stack cascade.

Reads cascade manifests and evaluates gates per D3.4. No external dependencies.

This is the standalone CLI parity surface for every gate's hook-side predicate.
Hooks call it on the auto-fire path; the founder calls it on the resume path;
tests call it on the smoke path. The same arg-shape and exit codes apply across
all three contexts.

The CLI surface (D3.4 §`solo-verify` CLI surface + spec AC-15):

  solo-verify onboard <product>          # onboard.* gates
  solo-verify specify <ticket>           # spec.* gates
  solo-verify review  <ticket>           # review.* gates
  solo-verify plan    <ticket>           # plan.* gates
  solo-verify update-linear <ticket>     # update-linear.* gates
  solo-verify build   <ticket>           # build.* gates (pre-flight + finalize)
  solo-verify wrap    <ticket>           # wrap.* gates
  solo-verify verify  <milestone>        # verify.* gates incl. per-child dispatch
  solo-verify retro   <milestone>        # retro.* gates

Hook-invocation aliases (D2.2 §Hook/script table):
  solo-verify subagent <agent_id>        # SubagentStop on four-hat agents
  solo-verify build-spawn   <ticket>     # PostToolUse on Ralph spawn
  solo-verify build-finalize <ticket>    # Stop on /build orchestrator
  solo-verify milestone <id>             # alias for `verify` from /verify hook

Flags:
  <stage> <ticket> --gate <gate-name>    # single-gate evaluation
  <stage> <ticket> --reconcile [--yes]   # re-derive expected state, repair drift
                                         # (F-Rev-2 carry-forward — also onboard/
                                         # update-linear/review/verify/retro)
  --list-gates [stage]                   # all gates or per-stage subset
  --explain <stage>.<gate-name>          # predicate text, halts, recovery

Exit codes (D3.4):
  0  All gates evaluated, all passed.
  1  One or more gates halted (standard halt).
  2  Stage / gate unknown; Python version too old; usage error.
  3  Manifest chain broken (provenance halt). Triggers `--reconcile` routing.
  4  Filesystem / Linear inconsistency that prevents evaluation
     (e.g. .cascade/manifests/ missing entirely).

Authored against D3.4 (gates), D2.1 v2 + v2.1 (trust model, run-state path),
D3.1 (decomposition strategies), D3.2 (pyramid shapes), D3.3 (perceptual /
invariance predicates), D4.0 (build & distribution), D4.5 (reconciliation
primitives).
"""

